Fixed and committed as 78a31e61; the message ends Fixes #1111. The seven verbs changelog, memories, docs, def, find, outline and grep now stop with exit 2 when given a dash-led word that isn't one of their own flags, and nothing runs. Before, find --bogus searched for the text --bogus, and docs --bogus asked docs.rs about a crate called --bogus.

How it works
• One rule for all seven: it lives in a new file, src/verb_flags.rs. The error message reuses the top-level one, so it reads error: unknown flag '--x' (did you mean …?) for \yoyo <verb>\. Nothing ran.
• grep's flags: they come from a new GREP_FLAGS list in commands_search.rs. A test checks that this list exactly matches the flags grep's own parser recognises. I checked the test works: removing --count from the list made it fail, and putting it back made it pass.
• Each verb's own flags: outline keeps --all. The other five take no flags. changelog now takes one optional count, like evolution, so changelog -5 and changelog foo are refused too.
• `--`: it still ends flag parsing, so yoyo find -- --weird-name searches for a name starting with a dash. grep's parser already handled --; for the other verbs the -- is now removed before the search runs.
• Small extra fix: outline --all x used to search for the text "--all x". It now treats a leading --all as the flag, the same as a trailing one.

Checks
• Built binary, in a temp git repo: all seven <verb> --bogus exit 2. These still run: grep -c TODO, grep -- --bogus, find -- --bogus, changelog, changelog 5, memories foo, outline main --all and def main. docs serde is only covered by a unit test, because I didn't want to make a network call.
• cargo build, cargo test, clippy -D warnings and fmt --check all pass.
• After the full test run I added a note to docs/src/usage/commands.md. Only the two test groups that read that file were re-run, and they pass.

Bookkeeping: src/dispatch_sub.rs grew by 37 lines, to 2640. I moved the logic and its tests into the new file to keep that growth down. The new sizes for it and commands_search.rs are recorded in tests/module_size.rs. git grep '#1111' found only history comments, no user-facing "see #1111" that needed changing.

Verdicts for the issue's other rows (no code changed):
• `test --bogus`: the arguments go straight to the project's own test runner by design (#745).
• `blame --bogus`: git refuses the option, exit 1.
• `review --bogus`: from reading the code, it fails with "file not found: --bogus" and exit 1 before any prompt is sent. I didn't run this one; it needs an API key set first.
